IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oas-core-periods`

-- Old Age Security Regulations (C.R.C., c. 1246), Part I (Applications): regulations 6 to 9, the money.
-- Reg 6 (an allowance of two dollars), reg 7 (rounding a partial monthly pension), reg 8 (the quarterly
-- adjustment of a benefit) and reg 9 (the average Consumer Price Index for a period of months).
--
-- Every figure that the Regulations take from the Act (the amount of a pension for the previous quarter, the
-- increase for a deferred application, the monthly Consumer Price Index figures that Statistics Canada
-- publishes) is a plain input, marked "out of range" with the section and the piece that encodes it.
-- Rounding is done with the shared helpers: the "third digit" rules of regs 7, 8(2), 8(3) and 9(2) decide on
-- one dropped digit, and a decision on one dropped digit (5 or more rounds up) is round-half-up.

§ `PART I Applications`

§§ `Payment of an Allowance Under Two Dollars`

-- src:59 | 6 Where a spouse, common-law partner or survivor is entitled under Part III of the Act to an allowance in an amount that does not exceed $2 monthly, an allowance of $2 is payable monthly to that spouse, common-law partner or survivor.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 6 (src:59)
GIVEN `the monthly amount of the allowance to which the person is entitled under Part III` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: section 19 (piece oa2) and section 21 (piece oa2)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 6: the allowance is raised to two dollars` `the monthly amount of the allowance to which the person is entitled under Part III` MEANS
        `the monthly amount of the allowance to which the person is entitled under Part III` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the monthly amount of the allowance to which the person is entitled under Part III` AT MOST 2

-- What is payable: two dollars where reg 6 raises it, otherwise the amount the person is entitled to (reg 6 says
-- nothing about an amount above two dollars, so it changes nothing there).
-- src:59 | 6 Where a spouse, common-law partner or survivor is entitled under Part III of the Act to an allowance in an amount that does not exceed $2 monthly, an allowance of $2 is payable monthly to that spouse, common-law partner or survivor.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 6 (src:59)
GIVEN `the monthly amount of the allowance to which the person is entitled under Part III` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: section 19 (piece oa2) and section 21 (piece oa2)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 6: the monthly allowance payable` `the monthly amount of the allowance to which the person is entitled under Part III` MEANS
    IF `reg 6: the allowance is raised to two dollars` `the monthly amount of the allowance to which the person is entitled under Part III`
    THEN 2
    ELSE `the monthly amount of the allowance to which the person is entitled under Part III`

§§ `Manner of Rounding Off Amount of Partial Monthly Pension`

-- src:62 | 7 Where the amount of a partial monthly pension referred to in subsection 3(3) of the Act, as increased under subsection 7.1(2) of the Act if applicable, contains a fraction of a dollar that is represented by three or more digits,
-- src:63 | (a) if the third digit is less than 5, the third and subsequent digits shall be dropped; and
-- src:64 | (b) if the third digit is 5 or greater than 5, the second digit shall be increased by 1 and the third and subsequent digits shall be dropped.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 7 (src:62-64)
GIVEN `the amount of the partial monthly pension before rounding` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: section 3(3) (piece oa1) and section 7.1(2) (piece oa1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 7: the amount of a partial monthly pension rounded off` `the amount of the partial monthly pension before rounding` MEANS
    `the amount of the partial monthly pension before rounding` `rounded half up to the number of decimal places` 2

§§ `Manner of Quarterly Adjustment of Benefit`

-- The five provisions of the Act under which a benefit is adjusted quarterly are the five subparagraphs of
-- reg 8(1)(a): a full monthly pension (7(2)), a supplement (12(2) and 12.1(3)) and an allowance (22(4.2) and 22.1(4)).
-- src:67 | 8 (1) When the amount of a benefit is adjusted quarterly under subsection 7(2), 12(2), 12.1(3), 22(4.2) or 22.1(4) of the Act,
-- src:68 | (a) there is a rounding off to the nearest cent, in accordance with subsection (2), of the product obtained by multiplying, as the case may be,
-- src:69 | (i) the amount referred to in paragraph 7(2)(a) of the Act by the ratio referred to in paragraph 7(2)(b) of the Act,
-- src:70 | (ii) the amount referred to in paragraph 12(2)(a) of the Act by the ratio referred to in paragraph 12(2)(b) of the Act,
-- src:71 | (iii) the amount referred to in paragraph 12.1(3)(a) of the Act by the ratio referred to in paragraph 12.1(3)(b) of the Act,
-- src:72 | (iv) the amount referred to in paragraph 22(4.2)(a) of the Act by the ratio referred to in paragraph 22(4.2)(b) of the Act, or
-- src:73 | (v) the amount referred to in paragraph 22.1(4)(a) of the Act by the ratio referred to in paragraph 22.1(4)(b) of the Act; and
-- src:74 | (b) any ratio referred to in paragraph (a) is expressed as a decimal number in accordance with subsection (3).
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 8(1) (src:67-74)
DECLARE `reg 8(1): Provision of the Act under which a benefit is adjusted quarterly` IS ONE OF
    `reg 8(1)(a)(i): subsection 7(2) of the Act`
    `reg 8(1)(a)(ii): subsection 12(2) of the Act`
    `reg 8(1)(a)(iii): subsection 12.1(3) of the Act`
    `reg 8(1)(a)(iv): subsection 22(4.2) of the Act`
    `reg 8(1)(a)(v): subsection 22.1(4) of the Act`

-- (3): a ratio of four digits after the decimal point is rounded to three. A ratio of two Consumer Price Index
-- figures usually has more than four digits; the encoding drops every digit after the fourth first, so the deciding
-- digit is the fourth either way (fork F-8(3) in NOTES.md).
-- src:78 | (3) Any ratio referred to in paragraph (1)(a) that is a decimal number represented by four digits after the decimal point is rounded as follows:
-- src:79 | (a) if the fourth digit after the decimal point is less than five, the fourth digit after the decimal point is dropped; and
-- src:80 | (b) if the fourth digit after the decimal point is five or greater than five, the third digit after the decimal point is increased by one and the fourth digit after the decimal point is dropped.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 8(3) (src:78-80)
GIVEN `the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: section 2 "Consumer Price Index" (piece oas-g0) and reg 9 below
      `the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: section 2 "Consumer Price Index" (piece oas-g0) and reg 9 below
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 8(3): the ratio of the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter to that for the second, expressed as a decimal number` `the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter` `the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter` MEANS
    IF `the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST ((`the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter` DIVIDED BY `the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter`) `rounded half up to the number of decimal places` 3)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (1)(a) and (2): the product of the amount and the ratio is rounded off to the nearest cent by the third-digit rule.
-- For subsection 7(2) the product is first increased under subsection 7.1(1) of the Act, if that applies (reg 8(2): "the
-- product obtained under subparagraph (1)(a)(i), as increased under subsection 7.1(1) of the Act, if applicable").
-- src:67 | 8 (1) When the amount of a benefit is adjusted quarterly under subsection 7(2), 12(2), 12.1(3), 22(4.2) or 22.1(4) of the Act,
-- src:68 | (a) there is a rounding off to the nearest cent, in accordance with subsection (2), of the product obtained by multiplying, as the case may be,
-- src:69 | (i) the amount referred to in paragraph 7(2)(a) of the Act by the ratio referred to in paragraph 7(2)(b) of the Act,
-- src:70 | (ii) the amount referred to in paragraph 12(2)(a) of the Act by the ratio referred to in paragraph 12(2)(b) of the Act,
-- src:71 | (iii) the amount referred to in paragraph 12.1(3)(a) of the Act by the ratio referred to in paragraph 12.1(3)(b) of the Act,
-- src:72 | (iv) the amount referred to in paragraph 22(4.2)(a) of the Act by the ratio referred to in paragraph 22(4.2)(b) of the Act, or
-- src:73 | (v) the amount referred to in paragraph 22.1(4)(a) of the Act by the ratio referred to in paragraph 22.1(4)(b) of the Act; and
-- src:74 | (b) any ratio referred to in paragraph (a) is expressed as a decimal number in accordance with subsection (3).
-- src:75 | (2) When the product obtained under subparagraph (1)(a)(i), as increased under subsection 7.1(1) of the Act, if applicable, or the product obtained under any one of subparagraphs (1)(a)(ii) to (v) contains a fraction of a dollar that is represented by three or more digits,
-- src:76 | (a) if the third digit is less than five, the third and subsequent digits are dropped; and
-- src:77 | (b) if the third digit is five or greater than five, the second digit is to be increased by one and the third and subsequent digits are dropped.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 8(1)(a) and 8(2) (src:67-77)
GIVEN provision IS A `reg 8(1): Provision of the Act under which a benefit is adjusted quarterly`
      `the amount referred to in paragraph (a) of that provision` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: sections 7(2)(a), 12(2)(a), 12.1(3)(a), 22(4.2)(a) and 22.1(4)(a) (pieces oa1 and oa2)
      `the ratio expressed as a decimal number` IS A NUMBER -- reg 8(3) above
      `the percentage increase under subsection 7.1(1) of the Act` IS A MAYBE NUMBER -- out of range: section 7.1(1) (piece oa1); read only for subsection 7(2)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 8(2): the amount of a benefit as adjusted quarterly` provision `the amount referred to in paragraph (a) of that provision` `the ratio expressed as a decimal number` `the percentage increase under subsection 7.1(1) of the Act` MEANS
    `the product` `rounded half up to the number of decimal places` 2
    WHERE
        `the product` MEANS
            CONSIDER provision
            WHEN `reg 8(1)(a)(i): subsection 7(2) of the Act` THEN
                CONSIDER `the percentage increase under subsection 7.1(1) of the Act`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN `the amount referred to in paragraph (a) of that provision` TIMES `the ratio expressed as a decimal number`
                WHEN JUST pct THEN (`the amount referred to in paragraph (a) of that provision` TIMES `the ratio expressed as a decimal number`) TIMES (1 PLUS pct)
            WHEN `reg 8(1)(a)(ii): subsection 12(2) of the Act` THEN `the amount referred to in paragraph (a) of that provision` TIMES `the ratio expressed as a decimal number`
            WHEN `reg 8(1)(a)(iii): subsection 12.1(3) of the Act` THEN `the amount referred to in paragraph (a) of that provision` TIMES `the ratio expressed as a decimal number`
            WHEN `reg 8(1)(a)(iv): subsection 22(4.2) of the Act` THEN `the amount referred to in paragraph (a) of that provision` TIMES `the ratio expressed as a decimal number`
            WHEN `reg 8(1)(a)(v): subsection 22.1(4) of the Act` THEN `the amount referred to in paragraph (a) of that provision` TIMES `the ratio expressed as a decimal number`

§§ `Determination of Average Consumer Price Index for Period of Months`

-- (1): the aggregate of the monthly figures divided by the number of months. A period of no months has no average.
-- src:83 | 9 (1) The average of the Consumer Price Index for Canada for a period of months shall be determined by dividing the aggregate of the Consumer Price Index for Canada, as published by Statistics Canada under the authority of the Statistics Act, for each month in that period by the number of months in that period.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 9(1) (src:83)
GIVEN `the Consumer Price Index for Canada for each month in the period` IS A LIST OF NUMBER -- out of range: section 2 "Consumer Price Index" (piece oas-g0); the figures are published by Statistics Canada
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 9(1): the average of the Consumer Price Index for Canada for a period of months` `the Consumer Price Index for Canada for each month in the period` MEANS
    IF null `the Consumer Price Index for Canada for each month in the period`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST ((sum `the Consumer Price Index for Canada for each month in the period`) DIVIDED BY (count `the Consumer Price Index for Canada for each month in the period`))

-- (2): the quotient is expressed to one decimal place, the second digit after the point deciding.
-- src:84 | (2) Where the quotient obtained pursuant to subsection (1) contains a fraction that is less than 1, such fraction shall be expressed as a decimal fraction of two digits after the decimal point and
-- src:85 | (a) the second digit after the decimal point shall be dropped if that digit is less than 5; or
-- src:86 | (b) the first digit after the decimal point shall be increased by one and the second digit shall be dropped if the second digit is 5 or greater than 5.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 9(2) (src:84-86)
GIVEN quotient IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 9(2): the quotient expressed as a decimal fraction of one digit` quotient MEANS
    quotient `rounded half up to the number of decimal places` 1

-- (1) and (2) together, for any period of months.
-- src:83 | 9 (1) The average of the Consumer Price Index for Canada for a period of months shall be determined by dividing the aggregate of the Consumer Price Index for Canada, as published by Statistics Canada under the authority of the Statistics Act, for each month in that period by the number of months in that period.
-- src:84 | (2) Where the quotient obtained pursuant to subsection (1) contains a fraction that is less than 1, such fraction shall be expressed as a decimal fraction of two digits after the decimal point and
-- src:85 | (a) the second digit after the decimal point shall be dropped if that digit is less than 5; or
-- src:86 | (b) the first digit after the decimal point shall be increased by one and the second digit shall be dropped if the second digit is 5 or greater than 5.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 9(1) and 9(2) (src:83-86)
GIVEN `the Consumer Price Index for Canada for each month in the period` IS A LIST OF NUMBER -- out of range: section 2 "Consumer Price Index" (piece oas-g0); the figures are published by Statistics Canada
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 9: the average of the Consumer Price Index for a period of months as determined under regulation 9` `the Consumer Price Index for Canada for each month in the period` MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 9(1): the average of the Consumer Price Index for Canada for a period of months` `the Consumer Price Index for Canada for each month in the period`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST quotient THEN JUST (`reg 9(2): the quotient expressed as a decimal fraction of one digit` quotient)

-- The two figures that the Act's ratio provisions take (the register of oas-core, item 11): the average for the three
-- months of the first, and of the second, adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter, determined as reg 9
-- says. The keel gives the exact mean of the three monthly figures (fork F10 there); reg 9(2) rounds it to one digit.
